{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "At the Bank"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Thank You, but I'm Not Interested"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately explain information about interests, hobbies, and preferences in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Making an Offer "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you are at the bank, bank tellers can make polite offers for a service or offer other forms of help.  When making offers, it is common to use  <span class=\"strong\">modals</span> like  <span class=\"italic\">would</span> or  <span class=\"italic\">can</span>. These are common expressions you hear:<br><br> <span class=\"italic\">Can I help you?</br> Would you be interested in applying for a credit card?</br> How about a travel card?</br> Would you like ... ?</span>"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Saying No Politely"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "In many countries, you cannot just say the word \"no\". You should be more polite. To politely say no, you can use expressions like:<br><br><span class=\"italic\"> No, that's OK. Thank you.<br> No, I'm fine. Thank you.<br> Thanks for the offer, but no thank you.<br> I appreciate the offer, but ... <br>   I'll pass, thank you.  <br/> I'm not interested right now.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Bank Teller</span>: Would you like to apply for a credit card?<br>  <span class=\"strong\">Customer</span>: Thanks for the offer, but no thank you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Notice that these expressions use the  <span class=\"strong\">Simple Present</span> tense."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to log in"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to type information in a website so you can use it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can log into the bank's website."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use at the bank."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "bank account"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an agreement between you and the bank where you make deposits  and take out money"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I'd like to open a bank account, please. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "account number"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a number used to identify an account"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Type in your account number to log in."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "password"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a secret group of letters and/or numbers  you must type in before you can log in"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Do I type in my password here?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "convenient"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "useful to you because it saves time"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: A credit card is convenient for travel. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "prepaid"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "paid before it is needed or used"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  This is a prepaid credit card."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to run low"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to near the end of an amount of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: When the amount starts to run low, you can add more money."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud07"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fund"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an amount of money available "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can add more when you run low on funds."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "currency"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the money that a country uses"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Remember to use the correct currency when travelling."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to reload"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to add more; to fill up"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can reload your card online. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn3le05ob03aud10"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn3le05ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read each role below and choose one."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Practice the situation with your partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Change roles."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Role 1:</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"t